    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d447-a4">

                <pb facs="0522" n="462" sameAs="frus:frus1895p1/pg462"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 4 in No. 329.—Telegrams.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Stern to Mr. Jackson</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >received August 6, 1895</hi>).</head>
                <dateline>[<date ana="#date_undated-inferred-from-document-head"
                        calendar="gregorian" type="received-date" when="1895-08-06"
                    >undated</date>]</dateline>
                <p>Verdict a surprise. While even prosecuting attorney proposed line, judge
                    pronounced two weeks’imprisonment and 600 marks. Do not know at present what
                    further steps I will take. Please advise me how embassy thinks about the
                    matter.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Louis Stern</hi></signed>.</closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p rendition="#center"><hi rendition="#italic">Embassy to Mr. Stern</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">sent August 6, 1895</hi>).</p>
                    <p>If appeal to higher court thought useless, your only recourse is to petition
                        for pardon. Sentence has been reported to State Department.</p>
                    <closer><hi rendition="#small-caps">Embassy</hi>.</closer>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
